  "query_preview": "..The surface high pressure system near the Four Corners \nwill support dry conditions, near to slightly above seasonable \ntemperatures, and north to northeast winds across northern AZ \nthrough Thursday. Looking towards Friday and the weekend, models \ncontinue to show a cut-off low breaking off of a deepening trough\noff of the west coast and moving across Baja California. Model \ntrends have backed off slightly on a more northerly track of the \nlow across southern AZ border and still show this low weakening \nas it does so. The current pattern predicted by the models would \nsupport some showers, isolated thunder and the potential for \ngusty winds over the weekend, particularly toward the White \nMountains. However, there is low confidence on this system having\nany more than minor impacts.\n\nBeyond the weekend, our attention will then turn toward the deep \nwest coast trough that originally creates the cut-off low,\nincreasing confidence for a cooling trend and precipitation early\nnext week. However, this is just beyond the current 7 day \nforecast period and confidence on any particular forecast detail \nfor this trough is low at this time.",
